## Django Models Guidelines

### ORM Usage

- Leverage Django's ORM for all database interactions
- Avoid raw SQL queries unless absolutely necessary for performance
- Use Django's built-in field types and validators
- Implement proper model relationships (ForeignKey, ManyToMany, OneToOne)

### Model Design

- Keep business logic in models using methods and properties
- Use descriptive field names following Python naming conventions
- Implement proper model validation using clean() methods
- Use Meta class for model configuration (ordering, indexes, constraints)

### Database Optimization

- Add database indexes for frequently queried fields
- Use select_related() for ForeignKey relationships
- Use prefetch_related() for ManyToMany relationships
- Implement database constraints for data integrity

### Content Models

- Design models for content management (videos, images, text)
- Implement proper file handling for media uploads
- Use ImageField and FileField with appropriate validators
- Consider content versioning and history tracking

### Transaction Models

- Design models for financial transactions and billing
- Implement proper decimal field usage for monetary values
- Use transaction atomic operations for data consistency
- Implement audit trails for transaction history

### User and Authentication

- Extend Django's built-in User model if needed
- Implement proper user roles and permissions
- Use Django's authentication framework
- Design models for user profiles and preferences
